      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Once in a lifetime opportunity on the verge of the Atlantic!\r\nExceptional 6 bedroom dormer bungalow in an extraordinary setting with breathtaking views as far as the eye can see.\r\n\r\nThere are homes that impress, and then there are homes that leave a lasting impression. Creevagh Heights is firmly in the latter category - an exceptional coastal residence occupying one of North Mayo's most spectacular settings, where uninterrupted views across the Atlantic Ocean stretch as far as the eye can see.\r\n\r\nSituated along the world-famous Wild Atlantic Way, this magnificent six-bedroom dormer bungalow presents a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to acquire a truly special home in an idyllic location where peace, privacy and breathtaking natural beauty combine to create an unforgettable property. From the moment you arrive, it is immediately apparent that this is no ordinary property. \r\n\r\nLacken stone features on the house, sheds and flower beds add charm and seamlessly blends the property into its surroundings. To the rear, the landscape gives way to an awe-inspiring panorama of the Atlantic Ocean, offering uninterrupted coastal views with nothing between you and the horizon. Whether enjoying a morning coffee as the sun rises over the sea, watching dramatic Atlantic sunsets, or simply listening to the soothing sound of the waves, every day here feels like a retreat from the ordinary. The atmosphere is one of complete serenity – peaceful, magical and impossible to replicate.\r\n\r\nExtending across an expansive footprint, the accommodation has been thoughtfully designed to provide both exceptional family living and excellent guest accommodation. The spacious interior comprises two elegant sitting rooms, a welcoming living room, dining room, kitchen, utility room, bathroom, storage room, hotpress, office space and six well-appointed bedrooms. Two bedrooms benefit from luxurious en-suite facilities, while a further two enjoy adjoining private shower rooms, making the layout ideal for family life or guest accommodation.\r\n\r\nHaving operated as a highly successful Bed & Breakfast for many years, the property offers enormous potential for those wishing to continue a hospitality business or simply enjoy an expansive family home in an unrivalled setting.\r\n\r\nPresented in true turnkey condition, the home offers an excellent standard of comfort throughout. Zoned oil-fired central heating with Climote smart controls allows heating to be managed remotely from your mobile phone, while a solid fuel stove and an open fireplace add warmth, comfort and timeless character.\r\n\r\nExternally there are storage sheds, an easily maintained concrete driveway and ample parking providing practicality alongside the property's undeniable charm. Access to high-speed fibre broadband in the area is particularly attractive to those wishing to work from home.\r\n\r\nWhile the setting offers complete peace and seclusion, the property remains convenient to nearby towns and villages. Ballycastle (10km), Killala (14km), and the thriving town of Ballina (26km) offer a range of supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, bars, schools, churches, pharmacies, transport links and everyday amenities.\r\n\r\nThe surrounding area is renowned for its outstanding natural beauty and rich heritage, making it one of Ireland's most sought-after coastal destinations. Some of Mayo's finest beaches, including Lacken Strand, Kilcummin Back Strand and Ross Beach, are all within easy reach, while the magnificent Enniscrone Beach and its championship golf course are just a little further along the coast. \r\n\r\nHistory enthusiasts will appreciate nearby Moyne Abbey, Rathfran Abbey and Rosserk Friary, while the internationally renowned Céide Fields and the dramatic sea stacks of Downpatrick Head showcase some of Ireland's most remarkable archaeological and geological treasures. The wider region offers endless opportunities for exploration, from the spectacular Belmullet Peninsula with its tidal pool and Carne Golf Links, to the scenic coastal walks and looped trails around Carrowteigue, ensuring there is always somewhere new to discover."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway \r\n2.8m (9'2\") x 1.93m (6'4\")\r\nBright entrance hall with a tiled floor, coving to the ceiling, and two south-west facing windows providing ample natural light.\r\n\r\nHallway \r\n1.04m (3'5\") x 6.29m (20'8\")\r\nBright hall with a tiled floor, coving to the ceiling. This leads to a bedroom and sitting room. Two large south-west facing windows provide ample natural light.\r\n\r\nHallway \r\n15.62m (51'3\") x 1.23m (4'0\")\r\nBright hall with a tiled floor, coving to the ceiling leading to all areas to the rear of the property.\r\n\r\nSitting Room \r\n6.22m (20'5\") x 3.48m (11'5\")\r\nLarge dual aspect room with fantastic views of the Atlantic Ocean. This room has laminate timber flooring, coving to the ceiling, and an open fireplace. A beautiful feature of this room is the statement picture window overlooking the ocean.\r\n\r\nUtility \r\n3.3m (10'10\") x 2m (6'7\")\r\nFunctional room to the front of the property with a tiled floor, fitted cabinetry and tiled splashback. A south-west facing window brings natural light to the space.\r\n\r\nKitchen \r\n4.22m (13'10\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\r\nBright kitchen with a tiled floor, fitted solid wood cabinetry with granite worktops, integrated ovens/hob and fridge and tiled splashback. Two large windows and a glass-panelled door provide ample natural light and superb views of the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nLiving Room \r\n7.89m (25'11\") x 3.67m (12'0\")\r\nSpacious room with a solid timber floor, coving to the ceiling, solid fuel stove with wooden mantlepiece and two large windows overlooking the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nDining Room \r\n4m (13'1\") x 4.1m (13'5\")\r\nWith a tiled floor, spotlights to the ceiling, and a large window overlooking the side garden and Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nBathroom \r\n3.16m (10'4\") x 2.52m (8'3\")\r\nFully tiled with a corner shower bath, toilet, pedestal sink, and two windows providing natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nOffice Area \r\n2.97m (9'9\") x 3.71m (12'2\")\r\nClever use of space at the base of the staircase with a tiled floor and coving to the ceiling.\r\n\r\nHotpress \r\n1.65m (5'5\") x 1.95m (6'5\")\r\nConvenient additional storage space with shelving at the end of the hallway.\r\n\r\nHallway \r\n1.54m (5'1\") x 3.85m (12'8\")\r\nLeading to the side door.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\n3.07m (10'1\") x 4.96m (16'3\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring and a large window overlooking the Atlantic Ocean. There is a walk-in wardrobe and ensuite adjoining.\r\n\r\nEnsuite \r\n1.94m (6'4\") x 3.37m (11'1\")\r\nFully tiled with a pedestal sink, toilet, and walk-in shower. A window provides natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe \r\n1.89m (6'2\") x 1.56m (5'1\")\r\nWith timber flooring, shelving and hanging rail.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\n3.15m (10'4\") x 2.79m (9'2\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, large window overlooking the side of the property, and a convenient ensuite.\r\n\r\nEnsuite \r\n1.43m (4'8\") x 3.02m (9'11\")Fully tiled with a pedestal sink, toilet, shower, and a window providing natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 \r\n3.27m (10'9\") x 3.4m (11'2\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, built-in wardrobes, and a large window overlooking the side of the property.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\n2.92m (9'7\") x 3.64m (11'11\")\r\nSingle room with timber flooring, built-in wardrobe, and a large window overlooking the side of the property.\r\n\r\nLanding \r\n1.77m (5'10\") x 6.27m (20'7\")\r\nThis leads to two bedrooms and two shower rooms.\r\n\r\nBedroom 5\r\n5.98m (19'7\") x 4.54m (14'11\")\r\nLarge double room with timber flooring, built-in wardrobes, vaulted ceiling, spotlights to the ceiling, two gable windows, and two velux windows providing magnificent views and natural light.\r\n\r\nShower Room 1\r\n2.07m (6'9\") x 2.65m (8'8\")\r\nFully tiled with a pedestal sink, toilet, shower, and velux window providing natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nBedroom 6\r\n4m (13'1\") x 3.97m (13'0\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, vaulted ceiling, and a velux window providing magnificent views and natural light.\r\n\r\nShower Room 2\r\n2.45m (8'0\") x 2.07m (6'9\")\r\nFully tiled with a pedestal sink, toilet, shower, and velux window providing natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nStorage Area\r\n1.25m (4'1\") x 2.89m (9'6\")\r\nConveniently located in the entrance hallway with shelving and hanging rail."
      },
